&lt;p&gt;OUR MISSION&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Redwood, we empower our customers with lights-out automation for their mission-critical business processes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;ABOUT US&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Redwood Software is the leader in full stack automation fabric solutions for mission-critical business processes. With the first SaaS-based composable automation platform specifically built for ERP, we believe in the transformative power of automation. Our unparalleled solutions empower you to orchestrate, manage and monitor your workflows across any application, service or server — in the cloud or on premises — with confidence and control.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Redwood’s global team of automation experts and customer success engineers provide solutions and world-class support designed to give you the freedom and time to imagine and define your future. Get out of the weeds and see the forest, with Redwood Software.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;CORE VALUES&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;One Team. One Redwood&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Make Your Own Weather&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Obsess over Customer Success&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work the Problem&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be Curious&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Own the Outcome&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respect Each Other&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;YOUR IMPACT&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We are seeking a Senior Deal Desk Analyst to join our Revenue Operations team. This role will primarily support our sales teams outside the United States, with a focus on EMEA. The Senior Deal Desk Analyst is responsible for providing crucial administration and operational support to the sales team in order to facilitate quote and order execution while enhancing efficiency. They will actively work with sales, legal, finance, and other cross functional teams on deal structuring and commercial terms to ensure compliance and optimize operational processes to drive successful order execution. They will act as an internal contact across functional back office teams to ensure that customer proposals are structured and processed according to the requests of the customer but also the company&#39;s policy. They will provide proactive guidance throughout the lifecycle of sales opportunities from the initial solution identification through closure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal review discussions with the Sales organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Legal, Finance, Product, and other departments to ensure that we are aligned with company policies, industry regulations and legal requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively drive quote and order execution through strategic deal structuring, ensuring they are delivered on time and within scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as first line support for any quote creation issues for the Sales Organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help advise and craft standards and best practices for all facets of a deal including product, operational, legal and financial.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential risks and issues during order creation and execution and develop mitigation plans to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide quote review and pricing approval support, ensuring compliance with company policy standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make recommendations for approvals for non-standard deal elements across internal stakeholders aimed at driving consistent terms and conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work proactively to predict and minimize potential issues before they arise and resolve those in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to streamline and improve quote and order execution processes, driving operational efficiency and effectiveness.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement quality control measures to ensure that deliverables meet the agreed-upon standards and quality criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate progress, issues, and key milestones to relevant stakeholders, including management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;YOUR EXPERIENCE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or global equivalent experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 - 5 years of experience in Sales Operations, Commercial support, or Finance role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3 - 5 year minimum experience using Salesforce.com, CPQ, Docusign CLM (or similar order creation/execution tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in deal structuring and execution and process governance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Quote and Order Form creation and special terms and conditions related to non-standard agreements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous improvement mindset with a focus on process optimization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have experience as a sales operations business partner, or related function, with cross functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with account management operations and data strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator with excellent written, verbal, and listening skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships effectively across global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and willingness to dig in with little direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence in advocating for best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent critical thinking skills with the ability to break down ambiguous problems into management components, think through solutions, and communicate clearly to all departments/stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong diagnostic and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to read, write, and speak fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;css-1i27f3a&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;css-ey7qxc&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;css-1s1axh3&quot; data-automation-id=&quot;jobPostingDescription&quot;&gt;
